course: dictionary
lesson: 3319
title: Evacuate: leaving danger behind
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To evacuate a place is to leave it because it is dangerous. To evacuate people is to move them to a safer place. You can read the clues around the word to work out what it means. «On 26 April 1986 reactor 4 of the Chornobyl nuclear power plant exploded» is a dangerous event, and later tens of thousands of people were moved away from it. So evacuated means moved out of danger.
explain: The Blitz sentence gives the clues: «many children were evacuated to the countryside with a gas mask and a label to live with strangers.» Children with gas masks and labels are being sent away from danger to somewhere safer. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence: "children were moved away to the countryside, with gas masks and labels" makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Schools practise fire drills so they can evacuate the building quickly and calmly. A drill is practice, so it helps everyone know what to do in a real emergency. The word evacuate is a verb, so it changes: evacuates, evacuated, evacuating. Look for phrases such as «be evacuated» and «evacuation drill», where evacuation is the noun for the whole action.
fact: Evacuate means to leave a dangerous place, or to move people out of it to safety.
fact: «Evacuated» is the past form, as in «were evacuated».
fact: An evacuation drill is practice for leaving a building quickly and calmly.
fact: During the Blitz, many British children were evacuated to the countryside, away from bombed cities.
fact: After the 1986 Chornobyl disaster, tens of thousands of people were evacuated for good.
exercise: «The fire alarm rang, so the class had to evacuate the building.» What does evacuate mean? | Paint the walls a bright colour | *Leave the building because it is dangerous | Stay inside and wait for lunch | Ring the bell again and again
exercise: In the Blitz, children were «evacuated to the countryside». Why were they sent away? | To go on a holiday at the seaside | To help the farmers pick apples all year | Because they had been naughty at school | *To keep them safe from bombs
exercise: Which word in «The town was evacuated before the flood» tells you the people were moved away? | *evacuated | before | flood | town
test: What is the purpose of an evacuation drill at school? | To practise singing in assembly | To practise writing long stories | *To practise leaving the building quickly and calmly | To practise eating lunch outside
test: «Tens of thousands were evacuated for good.» What does «for good» suggest? | They came back home the next day | They were given a prize for being brave | *They were moved away permanently | They went on a short trip to the seaside
exam: Which meaning fits evacuate in «Everyone must evacuate the cinema now»? | Buy a ticket and sit down | Sing a loud song together | Sit down and watch the film carefully | *Leave it quickly because it is unsafe
